.TH 7ZIPLX 1 "2026-11-24" "7zipLX 0.5.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
7ziplx \- native Linux GUI for the 7-Zip archive engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 7ziplx
.RI [ options ] " " [ path ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 7ziplx
is a single-pane archive manager with an optional second pane (F9), built with
Qt 6. It uses the portable 7-Zip engine for archive formats, compression,
extraction, testing, hashing and archive editing.
.PP
When
.I archive
is given, it is opened in the active panel after startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the application version.
.TP
.B \-\-extract-here
Extract each archive into the folder that contains it, then exit without
opening the main window.
.TP
.B \-\-extract-to-folder
Extract each archive into a new folder named after it (\fIphotos.tar.gz\fR
goes into \fIphotos/\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-extract-to " directory"
Extract the archives into \fIdirectory\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-extract
Show the Extract dialog for the archives.
.TP
.B \-\-test
Test the archives and report the result.
.TP
.B \-\-compress
Add all inputs to one archive next to them, named after the single input or,
for several inputs, after their folder.  An existing archive is updated after
asking.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " 7z|zip"
Archive format for \fB\-\-compress\fR (default 7z).
.TP
.BI \-\-compress-to " archive"
Add all inputs to \fIarchive\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-add
Show the Add to Archive dialog for the inputs.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Replace an existing archive instead of adding to it.
.TP
.B \-\-install-menus
Add the 7zipLX actions to the GNOME desktop and Files \fBScripts\fR menu
(\fI~/.local/share/nautilus/scripts/7zipLX\fR) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-remove-menus
Remove those actions and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/7zipLX/7zipLX.conf
Persisted window, panel and tool settings.
.TP
.I /usr/share/nautilus-python/extensions/7ziplx.py
The 7-Zip submenu of GNOME Files (needs python3-nautilus).
.TP
.I /usr/share/7ziplx/translations
Optional compiled Qt translation catalogs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 7z (1),
.BR 7zz (1)
.SH AUTHOR
7zipLX contributors.
